  "caption": "Quinn conquered the summit, then the walk down had the knees complaining and the next morning's stairs felt like a boss level.\n\nOn the way down, your thigh muscles act like brakes on every step, and the kneecap takes much more load on steep steps than on flat ground. That braking work is often why soreness peaks a day or two later.\n\nTrain the descent with stairs and controlled step-downs, add some single-leg balance work, carry the pack weight on the hip belt (poles can help), and tape hot spots before you set off.\n\nAn ankle you can't walk four steps on, a knee that swells quickly, locks or gives way, or numbness that won't settle is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
